            <ArticleTitle>[On hallucinations, bizarre sensations, phantom phenomena and body-image disturbances].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>600-2, 616</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subjective descriptions of neuropsychological phenomena which reflect body-image disturbances, are well known to neurologists, psychiatrists, neuropsychologists and rehabilitation medicine physicians. These phenomena may accompany patients with mental illnesses, after brain injury or with various neuro-orthopedic disabilities. It is also well documented in people who are exposed to extreme isolation or harsh situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
